{"id":"mahabharata-3-115","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":115,"title":"पञ्चदशाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 115 · Akritavrana on Rama Jamadagnya's birth","summary":{"en":"On Mount Mahendra, Rama Jamadagnya's disciple Akritavrana tells the story of Rama's origins: how Gadhi's daughter Satyavati married the sage Richika, and how a mix-up of the sacred porridges meant that her son Jamadagni would have a warrior's temper in his son.","kn":"ಮಹೇಂದ್ರಪರ್ವತದಲ್ಲಿ ಜಾಮದಗ್ನ್ಯ ರಾಮನ ಶಿಷ್ಯ ಅಕೃತವ್ರಣನು ರಾಮನ ಮೂಲದ ಕಥೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ: ಗಾಧಿಯ ಮಗಳು ಸತ್ಯವತಿ ಋಚೀಕ ಋಷಿಯನ್ನು ಮದುವೆಯಾದದ್ದು, ಪವಿತ್ರ ಚರುಗಳ ಅದಲುಬದಲಿನಿಂದ ಅವಳ ಮಗ ಜಮದಗ್ನಿಯ ಮಗನಲ್ಲಿ ಕ್ಷತ್ರಿಯ ಸ್ವಭಾವ ಬರುವಂತಾದದ್ದು.","hi":"महेन्द्र पर्वत पर जामदग्न्य राम के शिष्य अकृतव्रण राम के उद्गम की कथा सुनाते हैं: गाधि की पुत्री सत्यवती का ऋषि ऋचीक से विवाह, और पवित्र चरुओं की अदला-बदली के कारण उनके पुत्र जमदग्नि के पुत्र में क्षत्रिय स्वभाव आना।","te":"మహేంద్రపర్వతంపై జామదగ్న్య రాముని శిష్యుడు అకృతవ్రణుడు రాముని మూలకథ చెబుతాడు: గాధి కుమార్తె సత్యవతి ఋచీక మహర్షిని వివాహమాడడం, పవిత్ర చరువులు తారుమారవడం వల్ల ఆమె కుమారుడు జమదగ్ని కుమారునిలో క్షత్రియ స్వభావం రావడం.","ta":"மகேந்திர மலையில் ஜாமதக்ன்ய ராமரின் சீடர் அக்ருதவ்ரணர் ராமரின் தோற்றக் கதையைச் சொல்கிறார்: காதியின் மகள் ஸத்யவதி ருசீக முனிவரை மணந்தது, புனிதச் சருக்கள் மாறியதால் அவள் மகன் ஜமதக்னியின் மகனுக்கு க்ஷத்ரிய இயல்பு வந்தது.","ml":"മഹേന്ദ്രപർവതത്തിൽവെച്ച് പരശുരാമന്റെ ശിഷ്യനായ അകൃതവ്രണൻ, പരശുരാമന്റെ ഉത്ഭവകഥ പറയുന്നു: ഗാധിയുടെ മകൾ സത്യവതി ഋചീകമുനിയെ വിവാഹം ചെയ്തത്, പുണ്യപായസങ്ങൾ മാറിപ്പോയതിനാൽ അവരുടെ മകൻ ജമദഗ്നിയുടെ പുത്രന് ക്ഷത്രിയന്റെ സ്വഭാവമുണ്ടാകുമെന്ന്."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.115; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स तत्र तामुषित्वैकां रजनीं पृथिवीपतिः ।\nतापसानां परं चक्रे सत्कारं भ्रातृभिः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Staying there one night, the king and his brothers paid great honour to the ascetics."}},{"n":2,"text":"लोमशश्चास्य तान्सर्वानाचख्यौ तत्र तापसान् ।\nभृगूनङ्गिरसश्चैव वासिष्ठानथ काश्यपान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha told him of all those ascetics there: the Bhrigus, Angirases, Vasishthas and Kashyapas."}},{"n":3,"text":"तान्समेत्य स राजर्षिरभिवाद्य कृताञ्जलिः ।\nरामस्यानुचरं वीरमपृच्छदकृतव्रणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting them, the royal sage saluted them with joined hands and asked Akritavrana, Rama's follower and a hero:"}},{"n":4,"text":"कदा नु रामो भगवांस्तापसान्दर्शयिष्यति ।\nतेनैवाहं प्रसङ्गेन द्रष्टुमिच्छामि भार्गवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When will the blessed Rama show himself to the ascetics? On that occasion I wish to see the Bhargava.\""}},{"text":"अकृतव्रण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Akritavrana said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"आयानेवासि विदितो रामस्य विदितात्मनः ।\nप्रीतिस्त्वयि च रामस्य क्षिप्रं त्वां दर्शयिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama, who knows himself, already knows you have come. Rama is fond of you and will soon show himself."}},{"n":6,"text":"चतुर्दशीमष्टमीं च रामं पश्यन्ति तापसाः ।\nअस्यां रात्र्यां व्यतीतायां भवित्री च चतुर्दशी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ascetics see Rama on the fourteenth and the eighth days; when this night has passed the fourteenth will come."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"भवाननुगतो वीरं जामदग्न्यं महाबलम् ।\nप्रत्यक्षदर्शी सर्वस्य पूर्ववृत्तस्य कर्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You followed the mighty hero Jamadagni's son and were an eyewitness of all his past deeds."}},{"n":8,"text":"स भवान्कथयत्वेतद्यथा रामेण निर्जिताः ।\nआहवे क्षत्रियाः सर्वे कथं केन च हेतुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"So tell this: how were all the kshatriyas conquered in battle by Rama, and how and for what reason?"}},{"text":"अकृतव्रण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Akritavrana said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"कन्यकुब्जे महानासीत्पार्थिवः सुमहाबलः ।\nगाधीति विश्रुतो लोके वनवासं जगाम सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was in Kanyakubja a great and very mighty king known in the world as Gadhi, who went to live in the forest."}},{"n":10,"text":"वने तु तस्य वसतः कन्या जज्ञेऽप्सरःसमा ।\nऋचीको भार्गवस्तां च वरयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"While he lived in the forest a daughter, like an apsara, was born to him, and Richika of the Bhrigu line asked for her, Bharata."}},{"n":11,"text":"तमुवाच ततो राजा ब्राह्मणं संशितव्रतम् ।\nउचितं नः कुले किंचित्पूर्वैर्यत्संप्रवर्तितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king said to that brahmin of strict vows: \"A custom was established in our family by our forefathers."}},{"n":12,"text":"एकतःश्यामकर्णानां पाण्डुराणां तरस्विनाम् ।\nसहस्रं वाजिनां शुल्कमिति विद्धि द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Know, best of brahmins, that the bride-price is a thousand fast white horses with one black ear each."}},{"n":13,"text":"न चापि भगवान्वाच्यो दीयतामिति भार्गव ।\nदेया मे दुहिता चेयं त्वद्विधाय महात्मने ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And yet, Bhargava, the reverend one must not be told to pay it; this daughter of mine must be given to a great soul like you.\""}},{"text":"ऋचीक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Richika said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"एकतःश्यामकर्णानां पाण्डुराणां तरस्विनाम् ।\nदास्याम्यश्वसहस्रं ते मम भार्या सुतास्तु ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will give you a thousand fast white horses, each with one black ear; my wife will be your daughter."}},{"text":"अकृतव्रण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Akritavrana said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"स तथेति प्रतिज्ञाय राजन्वरुणमब्रवीत् ।\nएकतःश्यामकर्णानां पाण्डुराणां तरस्विनाम् ।\nसहस्रं वाजिनामेकं शुल्कार्थं मे प्रदीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Agreeing, king, he said to Varuna: \"Let a thousand fast white horses, each with one black ear, be given me for a bride-price.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"तस्मै प्रादात्सहस्रं वै वाजिनां वरुणस्तदा ।\nतदश्वतीर्थं विख्यातमुत्थिता यत्र ते हयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Varuna gave him a thousand horses, and the Ashvatirtha, where those horses rose, is famous."}},{"n":17,"text":"गङ्गायां कन्यकुब्जे वै ददौ सत्यवतीं तदा ।\nततो गाधिः सुतां तस्मै जन्याश्चासन्सुरास्तदा ।\nलब्ध्वा हयसहस्रं तु तांश्च दृष्ट्वा दिवौकसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At Kanyakubja on the Ganga he then gave Satyavati to him. Then Gadhi gave his daughter, and gods came as wedding guests, seeing the thousand horses obtained."}},{"n":18,"text":"धर्मेण लब्ध्वा तां भार्यामृचीको द्विजसत्तमः ।\nयथाकामं यथाजोषं तया रेमे सुमध्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Richika, best of brahmins, having won that wife by dharma, took pleasure in the slender-waisted woman as he wished."}},{"n":19,"text":"तं विवाहे कृते राजन्सभार्यमवलोककः ।\nआजगाम भृगुश्रेष्ठः पुत्रं दृष्ट्वा ननन्द च ॥","meaning":{"en":"After the wedding, king, the best of the Bhrigus came to see him with his wife, and delighted to see his son."}},{"n":20,"text":"भार्यापती तमासीनं गुरुं सुरगणार्चितम् ।\nअर्चित्वा पर्युपासीनौ प्राञ्जली तस्थतुस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The couple honoured him, their guru, seated and worshipped by the hosts of gods, and stood by with joined hands."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततः स्नुषां स भगवान्प्रहृष्टो भृगुरब्रवीत् ।\nवरं वृणीष्व सुभगे दाता ह्यस्मि तवेप्सितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the blessed Bhrigu, delighted, said to his daughter-in-law: \"Fortunate one, choose a boon; I will give what you wish.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"सा वै प्रसादयामास तं गुरुं पुत्रकारणात् ।\nआत्मनश्चैव मातुश्च प्रसादं च चकार सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She pleased that guru for the sake of a son, and he granted her wish and that of her mother as well."}},{"text":"भृगुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhrigu said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"ऋतौ त्वं चैव माता च स्नाते पुंसवनाय वै ।\nआलिङ्गेतां पृथग्वृक्षौ साश्वत्थं त्वमुदुम्बरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In your season, bathed, you and your mother should each embrace a tree for the sake of a son: you the fig tree, she the udumbara."}},{"n":24,"text":"आलिङ्गने तु ते राजंश्चक्रतुः स्म विपर्ययम् ।\nकदाचिद्भृगुरागच्छत्तं च वेद विपर्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, in the embracing they exchanged the trees. Once Bhrigu came and knew of the exchange."}},{"n":25,"text":"अथोवाच महातेजा भृगुः सत्यवतीं स्नुषाम् ।\nब्राह्मणः क्षत्रवृत्तिर्वै तव पुत्रो भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the very radiant Bhrigu said to his daughter-in-law Satyavati: \"Your son will be a brahmin who follows a warrior's way."}},{"n":26,"text":"क्षत्रियो ब्राह्मणाचारो मातुस्तव सुतो महान् ।\nभविष्यति महावीर्यः साधूनां मार्गमास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And your mother's son will be a great kshatriya who follows a brahmin's conduct, of great valour, following the path of the good.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"ततः प्रसादयामास श्वशुरं सा पुनः पुनः ।\nन मे पुत्रो भवेदीदृक्कामं पौत्रो भवेदिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then she appeased her father-in-law again and again: \"Let my son not be such; let it be my grandson.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"एवमस्त्विति सा तेन पाण्डव प्रतिनन्दिता ।\nजमदग्निं ततः पुत्रं सा जज्ञे काल आगते ।\nतेजसा वर्चसा चैव युक्तं भार्गवनन्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told \"So be it,\" she was pleased, Pandava. In due time she bore a son, Jamadagni, a delight of the Bhargavas, endowed with energy and brilliance."}},{"n":29,"text":"स वर्धमानस्तेजस्वी वेदस्याध्ययनेन वै ।\nबहूनृषीन्महातेजाः पाण्डवेयात्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Growing, radiant, great in energy through study of the Veda, he surpassed many sages, Pandava."}},{"n":30,"text":"तं तु कृत्स्नो धनुर्वेदः प्रत्यभाद्भरतर्षभ ।\nचतुर्विधानि चास्त्राणि भास्करोपमवर्चसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the science of archery came to him, best of Bharatas, and the four kinds of weapons, to him who shone like the sun."}}]}]}